course: dictionary
lesson: 7164
title: Seeing around corners
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A periscope is a long tube with mirrors at each end. It lets you see over or around something that is in the way. «A periscope uses two mirrors to let you see over things.» The mirrors catch light and send it along the tube to your eyes, so you can see what is out of sight.
explain: Light usually travels in straight lines. A periscope uses two mirrors to bend the path of light twice, so the light can go up, across and down again. «A periscope uses two mirrors to bend the path of light twice, so you can see over a wall or out of a submarine.»
explain: Submarines use periscopes to look above the sea while the rest of the submarine stays hidden under water. In science, you can build a simple periscope with two mirrors set at 45 degrees to see how light reflects.
fact: A periscope is a long tube with mirrors at each end.
fact: A periscope lets you see over or around something.
fact: Submarines use periscopes to look above the water.
fact: Light reflects off a mirror and bounces in a new direction.
fact: Two mirrors set at 45 degrees can bend light so you can see around a corner.
exercise: What is a periscope? | A boat that sails on rivers | A tube that makes sound louder | *A long tube with mirrors at each end | A small lamp with a glass shade
exercise: «A periscope uses two mirrors to let you see over things.» What does the periscope use to help you see? | Batteries | Wheels | Magnets | *Mirrors
exercise: Why does a submarine raise its periscope? | To catch fish for its crew | *To look above the sea while it stays hidden under water | To warm up its engine
test: Which two things does a periscope use to bend light? | Two wheels | *Two mirrors | Two lenses | A torch and a lamp
test: Name a place where a periscope is used. | A bicycle | A library shelf | A kitchen sink | *A submarine
exam: «A periscope uses two mirrors to bend the path of light twice.» What does bend mean here? | *Change the direction the light travels | Make the light go out | Make the light stop completely | Make the light brighter
